WEBVTT

00:00.800 --> 00:05.800
Okay, so this is the weekly invoice run. I do this every Friday morning
before ten, so it lands in their inbox the same day.

00:06.200 --> 00:10.000
New invoice. Now, the client name has to match exactly what's in the
accounting system, or it won't reconcile at the end of the month.

00:10.200 --> 00:14.500
This week it's Sunshine Cafe, four hundred and fifty for the weekly
social media package.

00:14.800 --> 00:18.000
Due date is always seven days out, whatever day you're actually doing this.

00:18.300 --> 00:25.500
Pop the description in and save. It gives you the invoice number there —
I jot that down if the internet's being flaky, saves tears later.

00:26.000 --> 00:32.500
Back on the list I mark it as sent. Oh — one big thing. If the amount is
over a thousand dollars, Kate has to approve it first. Email her before
you send anything big, don't just fire it off.

00:33.000 --> 00:37.500
Last bit, export the PDF and file it in the usual folder for the
accountant. And that's the whole thing. Ten minutes on a normal week.
